  "description": "No left-wall cupboard. A full-height cupboard on the back wall (x 0-900, 600 deep) with a pair of 437 doors, then a 400-wide, 330-deep open shelving tower (to x 1300), floor to ceiling, with five lit shelves. No base cupboards (no bench), so nothing on the back wall beyond. Inside, within its 18 boards (rear panels against the walls included): 864 × 582, 2407 high. A bookcase like the bedroom's (1490 wide, 290 deep, 1220 high) on the back wall, against the cupboards, 252 wider than the 1238 of clear wall beside the pine cupboard. The bedroom's pine cupboard (1300 wide, 500 deep, 1790 high) on the back wall, in the corner by the right-hand wall. A dresser on the front wall between the sink and the desk (x 823-2193): 1370 wide overall (its body 1330), 1940 high, 410 deep up to 830 (two drawers over two doors, under a wooden top), then 340 deep with three open shelves. The Ivar, lying on its side (830 long, 300 wide, 800 high), against the first radiator, 830 out into the room.From option 7 and the photo (new)",
